Callable after find_tools:
- search_worker — List workers (drivers), optionally narrowed by a name or code.
- list_driver_settlements — List driver pay settlements, the drivers' pay statements, newest period first.
- get_driver_settlement — Retrieve one driver settlement, a driver's pay statement, by id with its earnings, deduction and adjustment lines.
- get_worker_earnings_summary — Summarize what a worker has earned but not yet been paid on a settlement.
- get_settlement_dispute — Retrieve one pay dispute a driver raised on a settlement: its category, status, the driver's own description, the line it is about, and how it was resolved.
- generate_driver_settlement — Generate one driver's draft settlement for a pay period from the pay they have accrued, with their recurring earnings, deductions, escrow and advance recovery.
- generate_driver_settlement_batch — Generate the pay period's driver settlement batch: a draft settlement for every driver with accrued, unheld pay who has none for the period yet.
- attach_pay_events_to_settlement — Add a driver's accrued pay events to their draft driver settlement, such as a late load that missed generation.
- detach_pay_event_from_settlement — Take one load's pay off a draft driver settlement and return it to the unsettled pool, such as pay that belongs to the next period or is disputed.
- hold_driver_pay_event — Hold a driver's accrued pay for one load so it skips settlement until released, with the reason.
- release_driver_pay_event — Release a held driver pay event back into the pool the next settlement draws from.
- remove_driver_settlement_adjustment — Remove a manual adjustment line from a draft or pending driver settlement.
- recalculate_driver_settlement — Recalculate a draft driver settlement from what has accrued for its period, keeping manual adjustments.
- submit_driver_settlement — Submit a draft driver settlement for approval once its lines are right.
- approve_driver_settlement — Propose approving a driver settlement that is pending approval, which commits the organization to paying the driver what it comes to.
- reject_driver_settlement — Send a driver settlement that is pending approval back to draft, with the reason.
- post_driver_settlement — Propose posting an approved driver settlement to the general ledger.
- record_driver_settlement_payment — Propose recording that a posted driver settlement was paid, with how and the reference.
- void_driver_settlement — Propose voiding a driver settlement that is not yet paid, with the reason.
- pay_driver_now — Propose paying a driver now, off cycle, for pay they have accrued.
- list_carrier_settlements — List carrier settlements, the statements paying outside carriers for the loads they hauled.
- get_carrier_settlement — Retrieve one carrier settlement by id with its per-load cost lines: linehaul, fuel, accessorial and adjustments.
- generate_carrier_settlement_batch — Generate the pay period's carrier settlement batch, a draft settlement for each carrier with pending cost.
- remove_carrier_settlement_adjustment — Remove a manual adjustment line from a draft or pending carrier settlement.
- recalculate_carrier_settlement — Recalculate a draft carrier settlement from what has accrued for its period, keeping manual adjustments.
- submit_carrier_settlement — Submit a draft carrier settlement for approval once its lines are right.
- approve_carrier_settlement — Propose approving a carrier settlement that is pending approval, which commits the organization to paying the carrier what it comes to.
- reject_carrier_settlement — Send a carrier settlement that is pending approval back to draft, with the reason.
- post_carrier_settlement — Propose posting an approved carrier settlement to the general ledger.
- record_carrier_settlement_payment — Propose recording that a posted carrier settlement was paid, with how and the reference.
- void_carrier_settlement — Propose voiding a carrier settlement that is not yet paid, with the reason.
- list_edi_carrier_invoices — List freight invoices carriers sent over EDI, newest first, with how each reconciles: Unmatched, MappingRequired when no carrier is linked, Matched or Variance.
- accept_carrier_invoice_match — Propose accepting a carrier's invoice that matches what the load was expected to cost, clearing it for payment on the carrier's settlement.
- accept_carrier_invoice_match_with_variance — Propose accepting a carrier's invoice that differs from the expected cost and paying the difference.
- reject_carrier_invoice_match — Reject a carrier's invoice match that is wrong, such as an invoice for another load or a duplicate, with a note saying why.
- link_edi_carrier_invoice_to_carrier — Link an inbound EDI carrier invoice to the carrier in Trenova it came from, when its SCAC or DOT number did not find one, so it can be matched.
- list_pay_advances — List driver pay advances, the cash and money codes given against future pay, newest first.
- issue_pay_advance — Propose recording a cash or money-code advance a driver was given against future pay.
- write_off_pay_advance — Propose writing off what is still owed on a driver's pay advance, so no more is recovered from their pay, with the reason.
- list_escrow_accounts — List owner-operator escrow accounts with the driver, status and when each opened or closed.
- adjust_escrow_account — Propose a manual adjustment to an owner-operator's escrow balance, with what it is for.
- list_pay_codes — List the organization's active earning and deduction pay codes, each with the GL account it maps to.
- list_pay_profiles — List the organization's driver pay profiles, the packages that say how a driver is paid per mile, per load or by percentage.
- list_pay_assignments — List a driver's pay profile assignments, newest first: which profile paid them from when to when, their share of each load, and which one is in force today.
- list_recurring_deductions — List drivers' recurring deductions, such as insurance, equipment lease or escrow contributions.
- list_recurring_earnings — List drivers' recurring earnings, such as per diem, a guaranteed stipend or a bonus paid over time.

